<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narciso Clavería</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795–1851</span> · Also known as Narciso Clavería y Zaldúa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narciso Clavería was a Spanish general and Governor-General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1844 to 1849. In 1848 he led an expedition with steam gunboats that destroyed the strongholds of the Balangingi raiders in the Sulu archipelago. He is also remembered for his decree of 1849 that gave Filipino families standardised Spanish surnames from an official catalogue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narciso-claveria.jpg" alt="Narciso Clavería" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_teniente_general_Narciso_Claver%C3%ADa_y_Zald%C3%BAa,_conde_de_Manila_(Museo_del_Prado).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
